### Sivers and Collins Mechanism

The Sivers mechanism [15] is a model, where the transverse momentum (\(k_{\perp}\)) dependence of the PDF is correlated with the spin of the parent hadron, i.e.

\[f^{\uparrow}(x,k_{\perp})=f(x,k_{\perp})+\frac{1}{2}\tilde{\Delta}_{N}f^{ \uparrow}(x,k_{\perp})\hat{\cal P}\cdot\left(\hat{p}\times\hat{k}_{\perp} \right), \tag{1.9}\]

where, \(\hat{\cal P}\) and \(\hat{p}\) are the polarization and momentum direction, respectively, of the hadron. Isolating the PDF contribution to the asymmetry, one can consider

\[E_{C}\frac{d\sigma^{\uparrow}}{d^{3}\vec{p}_{C}}-E_{C}\frac{d \sigma^{\downarrow}}{d^{3}\vec{p}_{C}} \tag{1.10}\] \[= \sum_{a,b,c,d}\int dx_{a}d^{2}\vec{k}_{\perp a}dx_{b}d^{2}\vec{k} _{\perp b}dzd^{3}\vec{k}_{C}\delta\left(\vec{k}_{C}\cdot\hat{p}_{c}\right) \tilde{\Delta}_{N}\hat{f}_{a/A}^{\uparrow}\left(x_{a},\vec{k}_{\perp a},Q^{2}\right)\] \[\times\delta\left(\hat{s}+\hat{t}+\hat{u}\right)\frac{1}{z^{2}} J\left(z,|\vec{k}_{C}|\right)\hat{D}_{C/c}\left(z,\vec{k}_{C},Q^{2}\right).\]If \(\phi_{\cal P}\) and \(\phi_{k_{\perp}}\) are, respectively, the azimuthal angles around \(\hat{p}\) of \(\hat{\cal P}\) and \(\hat{k}_{\perp}\), then one can write

\[\tilde{\Delta}_{N}f\left(x,k_{\perp}\right) = f^{\uparrow}\left(x,k_{\perp}\right)-f^{\downarrow}\left(x,k_{ \perp}\right) \tag{1.11}\] \[= \tilde{\Delta}_{N}f^{\uparrow}\left(x,k_{\perp}\right)\hat{\cal P }\cdot\left(\hat{p}\times\hat{k}_{\perp}\right)\] \[= \tilde{\Delta}_{N}f^{\uparrow}\left(x,k_{\perp}\right)\sin\left( \phi_{\cal P}-\phi_{k_{\perp}}\right).\]

Thus, the \(k_{\perp}\) dependence produces an asymmetry in the PDF. The scattering of the asymmetrically distributed partons could then result in an azimuthal asymmetry in production of the jet or final-state hadron.

The Collins mechanism [16], on the other hand, considers the transverse momentum dependence of the fragmentation of a polarized scattered parton, \(c\), into a hadron, \(C\),

\[D\left(\vec{\cal P}_{c};z,\vec{k}_{\perp C}\right)=D\left(z,k_{\perp C}\right) +\frac{1}{2}\Delta D\left(z,k_{\perp C}\right)\vec{\cal P}_{c}\cdot\left(\hat{ p}_{c}\times\hat{k}_{\perp C}\right). \tag{1.12}\]

